<p>Use this tab to configure the options installed on the printer, and 
 register the available input trays and paper sizes.</p>
<p>Registration of paper sizes enables you to search for a printer loaded 
 with paper of a desired size using the Active Directory function of Windows.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="image" role="heading">Machine Image</p>
<p>Displays the printer configuration as an image.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" id="options" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Options</span></p>
<p>Select the options installed on the printer.<br/>
Whenever an option is added, select it in the <span class="Term-Soft">Options</span> 
 group. Even if an option is physically installed, it will not be available 
 for printing unless it is selected on this tab.</p>
<p>The <span class="Term-Soft">Punch Unit:</span> list is available when 
 an optional finisher with punch unit is installed and selected. Select 
 a type of punch unit in the list. Depending on the type of unit selected, 
 available punching positions will vary.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If the settings configured on this tab do not 
 match the physical configuration of the printer, you may get unexpected 
 print results.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Total Memory:</span></p>
<p>Specify the total size that is currently installed on the printer. Or 
 simply clicking <span class="Term-Soft">Update Now</span> configures the 
 current size of memory if the printer has bidirectional communication.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" id="tray" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray Settings</span></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Change Input Tray Settings...</span></p>
<p>Opens the <span class="Term-Soft">Change Input Tray Settings</span> dialog 
 box, where you can configure settings related to the paper in the paper 
 trays.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray Settings List:</span></p>
<p>Lists input trays and the size of paper loaded.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="auto" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Automatically Update Printer Information</span></p>
<p>Whenever you open the printer properties dialog box, this function queries 
 the printer for its configuration and automatically obtains information 
 about any options installed on the printer.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if bidirectional 
 communication between the printer and computer is established by network 
 or direct cable connection. For more information about bidirectional communication, 
 see the operating instructions provided with the printer. </p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="updatenow" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Update Now</span></p>
<p>Queries the printer for its configuration and automatically obtains 
 information about any options installed on the printer.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if bidirectional 
 communication between the printer and computer is established by network 
 or direct cable connection. For more information about bidirectional communication, 
 see the operating instructions provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this tab to the default settings.</p>
